\f1\fs22 Gerry searched for passageways and tunnels that were at least the size of the corridor he took from the concourse, backing his judgment that a viral research lab wouldn\'92t be reached by the first corridor from, say, a cafeteria or childcare centre. (Eloise, by reputation, provided the best employee benefits, even while selling more things that go boom than anyone else in the country.) He\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
 looked for corridors that curved south-east and had signs of light-cart traffic, but found no tyre marks, no scuffing, no evidence of minor collisions. The walls and floors were immaculate, even down to the little decals of random colour on the corners that brightened up the otherwise muted, functional d\'e9cor. As far as Gerry could tell, this was in the Goldilocks Zone of secret hideouts for evil arms dealers. Nothing was too bright or dim, and no colour was too pale or saturated. All the routes were curved; none were straight.\
