\f1\fs22 Gerry thought he heard singing; it abruptly stopped. It sounded like one of those Elvi tunes that had been flooding the music streams for months.\
The footsteps approached\'97of more people than Gerry could count, moving quietly though not stealthily. He stepped back from the junction, out of sight. A Jones appeared, pistol raised. Gerry waited for whoever had been singing. More Jones clones followed, spreading across the corridor. Behind them came Anthony Chantara with an Elvis, then a contingent of Elvi guarding the rear.\
\'93Good morning,\'94 Gerry said.\
\'93You will identify yourself,\'94 a Jones demanded.\
\'93Gerry Hardman, Commissioner of TRAMPS.\'94 Gerry knew claiming the title should trigger the clones\'92 tendency to defer to authority. \
\'93You will lower your weapon in the presence of Chanta, heir of Hardy Industries,\'94 a Jones ordered Gerry.\
\'93I will do no such thing. I am Commissioner of police and a PAPER agent. You will comply with my orders. Apprehend Chantara and the Elvi.\'94 Gerry looked at Chanta. \'93Anthony Chantara, I am arresting you for sedition and inciting rebellion.\'94\
The Jones clones wavered in the face of authority. The Elvi pointed their weapons at the clones. The clones pointed at the Elvi.\
Gerry saw no gun was trained on him. One bullet in Chantara\'92s head could end this. Gerry would keep out of it until the clones and the Elvi had mostly taken each other down, and he could mop up from the side once the shooting had died down.\
Chanta stepped into the path of impending gunfire between the Jones clones and the Elvi, which suited Gerry just fine. With his hands raised he faced the clones and said, \'93It isn\'92t deep. It\'92s mycelial.\'94\
Gerry couldn\'92t have guessed that Chanta\'92s enigmatic statement would move the clones\'92 collective apophenic minds from deep state to mushrooms to Grayling Corporation to PAPER to Government.\
To Gerry.\
Gerry couldn\'92t have guessed 
